      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4ad23cb1f6d87b1fb13a874865340c30087dcfd8db2da85b5b4f22cd45ca86cc",
      "text": "Breakfast, then a tour of the Brazilian side of the falls, in a national park of unique flora and fauna: “big water” in the Guaraní language, some 275 cascades, each with its own name, thunder into the Devil’s Throat gorge, a spectacle you could contemplate for hours.\n\nOptional: the Macuco Safari (USD 135 per person), about 3 km through the jungle in an open jeep, then on foot to the river and by motorboat close to the falls; the Bird Park (USD 65 per person); or a helicopter flight over the falls (USD 170 per person).",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
        "fileId": "1J-T_oASR49ex-y5KLtkmroop29Ht-g0S",
        "documentSha256": "18020884060aa6ecc4683f20840290a3298f6c039bbfde810458aa4232496fbf",
